Package: folio-draw
Version: 1.11.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: 20000
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, libxcb1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libwayland-client0, folio-fonts
Recommends: cups-client, xdg-utils, fonts-dejavu-core
Maintainer: Ron Shillings <ron.shillings@gmail.com>
Description: pictures, with layers and machine embroidery
 Folio Draw is a quick, uncluttered picture editor in the spirit of the classic
 desktop paint program: pencil, brushes, shapes, text, fill, selections, crop,
 resize and rotate, plus layers, blend modes and real transparency. It opens
 and saves PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF, WebP, TIFF, Windows icons, Photoshop PSD and
 OpenRaster (.ora, which keeps the layers); an animated GIF or WebP opens with
 one frame per layer. Embroidery: a picture becomes editable shapes with fill,
 satin and running stitches, lettering from a font, a density view and a
 stitch-out simulator, and saves for the machine as PES, DST, JEF, EXP, VP3,
 XXX or PEC. Every codec and the embroidery planner are its own, with no image
 library. Everything stays on this computer.
